1
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
"Boy, with Caution"

2
00:01:08,958 --> 00:01:10,708
You gave it to him on purpose, didn't you?

3
00:01:11,958 --> 00:01:13,458
Those pills.

4
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:18,250
Yes.

5
00:01:18,958 --> 00:01:20,208
Why?

6
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,208
Because he leaked the chat logs

7
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:28,125
and put you in a tough spot.

8
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:30,458
And you thought you'd
just get away with this?

9
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:40,958
What on earth do you want me to do?

10
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,333
It's nothing like that.

11
00:01:44,458 --> 00:01:45,875
Just tell me the truth.

12
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,250
Whatever it is, I'll do it.

13
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:57,125
Am I even allowed to
ask for anything from you?

14
00:02:00,125 --> 00:02:01,417
Besides,

15
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:06,083
you already said I don't
mean that much to you.

16
00:02:07,542 --> 00:02:09,708
So were you just testing me?

17
00:02:12,292 --> 00:02:14,250
You just wanted to see
how much you mean to me,

18
00:02:15,208 --> 00:02:17,728
and what it would take for me
to throw everything away for you?

19
00:02:18,417 --> 00:02:20,250
"Fine. I admit it that I wavered."

20
00:02:20,375 --> 00:02:22,809
Were you just trying to test my
feelings so you'd make me admit this?

21
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:24,042
Why would I do that?

22
00:02:28,875 --> 00:02:30,958
There's nothing wrong from wanting to

23
00:02:31,083 --> 00:02:32,625
hear these words from you.

24
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:35,900
I already told you.

25
00:02:36,594 --> 00:02:38,594
I see to it until the end.

26
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,590
That's just how it is, I...

27
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:43,450
I just give everything I can.

28
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:50,900
Why are you mad?

29
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,650
Like you said, I'm nothing to you.

30
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:59,290
You don't even feel
anything, nor do you waver...

31
00:02:59,458 --> 00:03:00,875
I was wavering.

32
00:03:07,292 --> 00:03:09,417
You made me waver.

33
00:03:10,917 --> 00:03:14,000
When you keep pushing me like
this, how could I not be shaken?

34
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,458
You don't want anything from me?

35
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:18,792
You have to.

36
00:03:19,458 --> 00:03:21,417
Even if you don't, make something up.

37
00:03:22,583 --> 00:03:25,875
That way, I'll have an
excuse to walk away from you.

38
00:03:29,625 --> 00:03:32,167
Is that what you really want?

39
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:35,125
Do you just want me to stop?

40
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:47,167
Because I really can't do it.

41
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,583
If I knew how...

42
00:03:52,292 --> 00:03:54,000
I'd do what you're asking of me.

43
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:59,500
But I really don't know
how to stop feeling like this.

44
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,600
Hyeon-jae.

45
00:04:09,542 --> 00:04:11,000
Let's end this here.

46
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:16,417
Stop using your situation to make me waver.

47
00:04:17,917 --> 00:04:19,625
I'm begging you, let's stop.

48
00:04:36,583 --> 00:04:37,917
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,375
Can't we just...

50
00:04:47,292 --> 00:04:49,250
keep going the way we are now?

51
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:58,333
I promise I really won't
ask for anything more.

52
00:05:00,958 --> 00:05:08,250
"Boy, with Caution"
(Final Episode)

53
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:25,417
Step out, please.

54
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:30,625
Your mother has already been discharged.

55
00:05:45,292 --> 00:05:47,042
Where is my mom right now?

56
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:04,125
Where did you transfer her?

57
00:06:05,042 --> 00:06:06,333
I'm not quite sure.

58
00:06:07,708 --> 00:06:09,667
Are you really using
this to threaten me now?

59
00:06:09,792 --> 00:06:12,875
You have a weakness I can
exploit, yet you still dare to defy me?

60
00:06:14,583 --> 00:06:15,917
You're going to be expelled.

61
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:20,643
Haven't you been begging
me to expel you this whole time?

62
00:06:20,667 --> 00:06:23,875
Isn't that why you caused
a mess too big to clean up?

63
00:06:31,083 --> 00:06:34,208
Have you finally figured out
what you can't afford to lose?

64
00:06:35,375 --> 00:06:38,292
If you want to know where
your mother is, you have two days

65
00:06:38,417 --> 00:06:39,937
to put everything back the way it was.

66
00:06:41,417 --> 00:06:42,708
Go ahead and try.

67
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:47,542
I'll make sure I become
a stain on your life

68
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:49,792
that you can never wipe clean.

69
00:06:51,458 --> 00:06:55,500
With that alone, I can
make you lose everything.

70
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,042
The things you don't want to lose

71
00:07:01,875 --> 00:07:03,667
must be too many to count.

72
00:07:07,917 --> 00:07:09,167
Dong-jin.

73
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:13,583
Get this brat out of my sight.

74
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:19,518
I'm handing out the mock exam results. Come up when I
call your name. (2027 Academic Year Mock Exam Report Card)

75
00:07:19,542 --> 00:07:20,667
Kim Ga-young.

76
00:07:27,968 --> 00:07:28,968
(Lee Hyeon-jae)

77
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,125
Lee Hyeon-jae.

78
00:07:44,042 --> 00:07:46,250
Next, Joo Young-ji.

79
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:54,833
I sent you the evaluation form
for the disciplinary committee.

80
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:57,083
Just fill it out roughly
and send it back to me.

81
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:04,042
Hyeon-jae didn't come
to school today, did he?

82
00:08:04,167 --> 00:08:05,458
I haven't seen him around.

83
00:08:08,375 --> 00:08:11,125
Just mark it as sick leave, like usual.

84
00:08:12,125 --> 00:08:14,625
For the evaluation, just write down

85
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,375
exactly what the students said.

86
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,083
As for what happened between
him and Young-moon before,

87
00:08:19,208 --> 00:08:21,500
don't go out of your way to bring that up.

88
00:08:26,875 --> 00:08:32,250
(Student Disciplinary Committee)

89
00:08:41,458 --> 00:08:44,500
Keep a close eye on him
until the committee meets.

90
00:08:44,625 --> 00:08:46,542
Don't let Hyeon-jae cause any more trouble.

91
00:08:48,792 --> 00:08:50,672
What kind of punishment
do you think he'll get?

92
00:08:51,792 --> 00:08:54,375
First there was the bullying
incident with Young-moon,

93
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,220
and now this pill incident with Hyeon-jong.

94
00:08:56,583 --> 00:08:58,463
He's looking at a
suspension at the very least.

95
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:02,125
Keeping the rumors from
spreading is better for you, too.

96
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,417
Especially after those leaked chat logs.

97
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:12,500
Why did that kid have to go

98
00:09:12,625 --> 00:09:14,905
and make a scene in front
of another parent? Seriously...

99
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:18,958
Because I really can't do it.

100
00:09:19,083 --> 00:09:23,125
But I really don't know
how to stop feeling like this.

101
00:09:27,375 --> 00:09:30,583
I doubt even the
Chairman can bury this one.

102
00:09:32,542 --> 00:09:34,333
He won't cause any more trouble.

103
00:09:37,958 --> 00:09:39,250
Not anymore.

104
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,700
I'm sorry, I haven't submitted
the evaluation form yet.

105
00:09:53,167 --> 00:09:55,333
You can just hand it in tomorrow.

106
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,708
Please take a look at this first.

107
00:10:09,625 --> 00:10:11,167
(Letter of Resignation)

108
00:10:43,167 --> 00:10:44,875
Do you have anything else to wrap up?

109
00:10:57,458 --> 00:10:58,978
You're heading to the hospital, right?

110
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Keep avoiding me all you want.
I'm gonna keep following you.

111
00:11:09,125 --> 00:11:11,417
Don't you remember what I told you?

112
00:11:11,542 --> 00:11:12,917
You said you liked me.

113
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:15,750
You never said you were going to avoid me.

114
00:11:17,292 --> 00:11:19,167
It means the same thing. Save your breath.

115
00:11:19,583 --> 00:11:21,917
If I don't try this hard, you
won't even look my way.

116
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,750
So this is what I used to be like.

117
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:31,500
If you want to keep
following me, suit yourself.

118
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,720
I'm just going to keep avoiding you anyway.

119
00:11:57,792 --> 00:11:59,458
Looks like you've been waiting for me.

120
00:12:16,792 --> 00:12:18,500
You didn't even know when I'd show up.

121
00:12:29,792 --> 00:12:33,375
Mr. Jang, I don't want to stop.

122
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:38,125
And I'm not going to.

123
00:12:41,917 --> 00:12:43,792
Did you wait here just to tell me that?

124
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:48,458
Yes.

125
00:12:54,833 --> 00:12:56,708
You're not...

126
00:12:59,792 --> 00:13:01,750
going to abandon me either, right?

127
00:13:06,583 --> 00:13:08,000
Right?

128
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,750
Nothing ever even started between us.

129
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,333
Go home.

130
00:13:26,917 --> 00:13:29,042
It's way too hot out.

131
00:13:49,083 --> 00:13:50,917
Your friend was right.

132
00:13:51,375 --> 00:13:54,208
Fruit tastes sweeter when you
leave it out at room temperature.

133
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:57,167
Don't eat too much before bed.

134
00:13:59,375 --> 00:14:00,458
Geez, stop nagging.

135
00:14:00,583 --> 00:14:02,042
Here, have a bite.

136
00:14:04,375 --> 00:14:05,583
Grandma.

137
00:14:06,042 --> 00:14:07,292
Yeah?

138
00:14:10,083 --> 00:14:11,583
Park Sung-won...

139
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:15,792
Grandma, did you say something to him?

140
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:21,375
Did you tell him we
come from different worlds,

141
00:14:22,792 --> 00:14:24,542
and that he shouldn't get too close to me?

142
00:14:24,667 --> 00:14:26,000
I did.

143
00:14:28,083 --> 00:14:29,375
Why would you say that?

144
00:14:30,458 --> 00:14:33,625
Because it's true. I
was just stating a fact.

145
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,250
I'm so ashamed of myself.

146
00:14:39,792 --> 00:14:44,542
Everyone in this world lives differently.

147
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:49,417
There are as many ways
to live as there are people.

148
00:14:50,875 --> 00:14:53,917
Just because you two grew
up in different circumstances,

149
00:14:54,542 --> 00:14:56,583
is that something to be ashamed of?

150
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,250
No, it's not that.

151
00:15:04,625 --> 00:15:07,833
To protect my own pride,
I kept pushing him away.

152
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:12,667
It turns out I had it all wrong.

153
00:15:14,875 --> 00:15:16,583
That's why I'm so ashamed.

154
00:15:18,833 --> 00:15:20,792
I was just blaming
someone else this whole time.

155
00:15:24,083 --> 00:15:25,958
More than being broke,

156
00:15:27,292 --> 00:15:30,532
more than having to beg for money to pay
your hospital bills after you collapsed,

157
00:15:34,292 --> 00:15:37,167
and more than all the crazy
things I did just to make a buck...

158
00:15:39,583 --> 00:15:41,023
This makes me feel way more ashamed.

159
00:16:38,667 --> 00:16:41,542
Is there a specific
reason you're resigning?

160
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:48,375
I know Class 2 has
caused plenty of trouble,

161
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:53,833
but you only have a few
months left on your contract.

162
00:16:55,833 --> 00:17:01,958
It's because... I know the reason...

163
00:17:05,208 --> 00:17:06,750
why Hyeon-jae is "out sick."

164
00:17:19,458 --> 00:17:21,218
Thank you for everything
you've done for me.

165
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:39,125
Out of my way.

166
00:17:48,417 --> 00:17:51,458
Have you heard anything
about the disciplinary action?

167
00:17:52,958 --> 00:17:55,417
Come to think of it, isn't
this whole mess your fault?

168
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:02,500
What are you doing? Sit down.

169
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:10,363
I'll be overseeing morning
study hall for the time being.

170
00:18:10,458 --> 00:18:11,792
Got it?

171
00:18:12,042 --> 00:18:13,292
Class President.

172
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:19,083
For now, bring any class issues or
forms that need to be turned in to me.

173
00:18:19,208 --> 00:18:20,417
Okay.

174
00:18:21,542 --> 00:18:24,958
I'll be filling in until a new
homeroom teacher is assigned.

175
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:26,417
What about Mr. Jang?

176
00:18:28,125 --> 00:18:30,292
I'll let you know once
everything is finalized.

177
00:18:30,417 --> 00:18:32,667
Alright, let's take attendance.

178
00:18:34,083 --> 00:18:35,417
Kim Ga-young.

179
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:38,667
Kim Min-jung.

180
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:45,458
Go ahead, keep avoiding me.

181
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:47,750
Didn't you tell me to suit myself?

182
00:18:49,875 --> 00:18:53,333
Even if you run and hide,
I'll find you no matter what.

183
00:18:53,458 --> 00:18:54,792
So keep running.

184
00:18:56,333 --> 00:18:57,726
How long are you going to keep this up?

185
00:18:57,750 --> 00:18:59,792
Until you stop avoiding me.

186
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,833
By the way,

187
00:19:04,583 --> 00:19:07,208
are you having dinner with
your grandma again tonight?

188
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:09,083
Yeah.

189
00:19:12,375 --> 00:19:14,000
Then have dinner with me tomorrow.

190
00:19:15,042 --> 00:19:16,333
I don't want to.

191
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:17,833
I reject you rejecting me.

192
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:18,583
Hey.

193
00:19:18,708 --> 00:19:20,375
At least give me a little time.

194
00:19:23,583 --> 00:19:25,143
Just spare a little bit of time for me.

195
00:19:25,750 --> 00:19:27,250
Give me...

196
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,542
some time to start liking you.

197
00:19:43,875 --> 00:19:45,417
I won't run away anymore.

198
00:20:21,208 --> 00:20:23,458
(Jang Gi-woo)

199
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:27,208
What's going on?

200
00:20:28,125 --> 00:20:29,542
Do you need something?

201
00:20:35,708 --> 00:20:37,167
I'd like to leave early today.

202
00:20:58,625 --> 00:21:00,000
Mr. Jang.

203
00:21:01,583 --> 00:21:03,708
Let's talk face-to-face.

204
00:21:05,208 --> 00:21:06,583
Mr. Jang!

205
00:21:13,708 --> 00:21:15,042
Mr. Jang!

206
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:35,125
When a client resists change,

207
00:21:35,250 --> 00:21:37,667
our first instinct is
usually to persuade them.

208
00:21:38,750 --> 00:21:43,125
However, in counseling, resistance
isn't an emotion that must be eliminated.

209
00:21:43,542 --> 00:21:48,333
The key lies in understanding what they are
trying so hard to protect by resisting change.

210
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,333
(Career Counselor Certification)

211
00:22:07,042 --> 00:22:09,333
(Class 3-2, Kim Jeong-ha)

212
00:22:19,792 --> 00:22:21,750
Is this Mr. Jang Gi-woo?

213
00:22:24,667 --> 00:22:26,042
What happened?

214
00:22:26,792 --> 00:22:28,000
Please help me.

215
00:22:35,042 --> 00:22:36,792
(Medical Bill Receipt)

216
00:22:41,542 --> 00:22:42,833
I'll pay you back.

217
00:22:44,958 --> 00:22:46,250
Don't worry about it.

218
00:22:55,292 --> 00:22:56,667
You did the right thing

219
00:22:58,417 --> 00:23:00,125
by calling me.

220
00:23:05,458 --> 00:23:07,125
Mr. Jang, why did you quit?

221
00:23:10,250 --> 00:23:11,792
I just...

222
00:23:12,792 --> 00:23:14,667
didn't think I could hold on any longer.

223
00:23:15,708 --> 00:23:17,542
That scumbag Choi Young-moon...

224
00:23:18,083 --> 00:23:21,333
He was going to rat out Kim Ji
Tae and pin the whole thing on him.

225
00:23:21,458 --> 00:23:23,083
Instead, he showed up at school

226
00:23:25,208 --> 00:23:27,518
and told them Choi Young-moon
was the one selling the pills.

227
00:23:27,542 --> 00:23:30,822
I heard he even got on his knees in the
faculty office and begged for forgiveness.

228
00:23:34,583 --> 00:23:36,333
Word is, he won't be expelled.

229
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:39,250
I mean Hyeon-jae.

230
00:23:43,167 --> 00:23:44,542
That's a relief.

231
00:23:45,792 --> 00:23:47,708
I figured you'd want to know.

232
00:23:52,208 --> 00:23:54,833
The Chairman might actually
beat Hyeon-jae to death.

233
00:23:56,875 --> 00:23:58,833
I've seen him get beaten with my own eyes.

234
00:24:01,042 --> 00:24:03,542
I used to wonder why
someone who had so much

235
00:24:03,667 --> 00:24:05,833
would choose to live like that.

236
00:24:09,708 --> 00:24:11,000
Now, I think I get it.

237
00:24:19,542 --> 00:24:21,667
Even though he has so much,

238
00:24:22,958 --> 00:24:24,678
there's nothing he can actually hold on to.

239
00:24:41,917 --> 00:24:43,417
You're back?

240
00:24:43,542 --> 00:24:45,708
I ordered fried chicken. Want some?

241
00:24:45,833 --> 00:24:47,125
Sure.

242
00:24:47,250 --> 00:24:48,708
Let me go change first.

243
00:24:57,667 --> 00:24:58,667
Look.

244
00:25:01,375 --> 00:25:03,125
I found it in the room.

245
00:25:03,875 --> 00:25:05,458
You thought you lost it, didn't you?

246
00:25:09,167 --> 00:25:10,887
You have something on your mind, don't you?

247
00:25:12,292 --> 00:25:13,875
You never drink unless something's up.

248
00:25:16,333 --> 00:25:18,917
You know what? Sometimes
you really leave me speechless.

249
00:25:19,708 --> 00:25:21,042
Ji-young.

250
00:25:23,292 --> 00:25:25,583
I'm not staying the night.

251
00:25:25,708 --> 00:25:27,875
I don't care if you're
comfortable with it or not.

252
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:29,292
I just don't want to.

253
00:25:35,083 --> 00:25:36,292
Let's get a divorce.

254
00:25:39,625 --> 00:25:41,583
Isn't that what you came here to say?

255
00:25:45,708 --> 00:25:48,208
Print out the papers and send them over.

256
00:25:49,208 --> 00:25:50,875
I don't have time to deal with it.

257
00:26:00,208 --> 00:26:03,750
I honestly thought you'd
never bring up divorce first,

258
00:26:03,875 --> 00:26:06,208
unless I shoved the
papers right in your face.

259
00:26:10,125 --> 00:26:13,285
Turning a blind eye, pretending not to
know, acting like everything was fine...

260
00:26:14,958 --> 00:26:16,667
I realized I was being way too cruel.

261
00:26:19,167 --> 00:26:20,542
Cruel to who?

262
00:26:27,250 --> 00:26:29,583
Why can't you answer?

263
00:26:30,958 --> 00:26:32,792
To yourself, obviously!

264
00:26:33,875 --> 00:26:35,167
You're right.

265
00:26:36,750 --> 00:26:38,750
I only cared about making
things easier on myself.

266
00:26:40,667 --> 00:26:43,167
Everyone does that.

267
00:26:46,083 --> 00:26:47,603
All I'm saying is, you did a good job.

268
00:27:12,917 --> 00:27:14,583
What are you, a teacher?

269
00:27:22,125 --> 00:27:23,667
Make sure you keep it on from now on.

270
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:30,580
(Amuna)

271
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:33,080
(Mr. Regret! Welcome back.
Do you want to start a new chat?)

272
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:50,292
I thought about it all night.

273
00:27:58,542 --> 00:28:01,500
If it's wrong to have these feelings...

274
00:28:14,833 --> 00:28:17,000
Why you didn't accept
what I'm giving you...

275
00:28:43,792 --> 00:28:45,458
When your heart is already wavering...

276
00:28:48,583 --> 00:28:50,167
Since you already swayed...

277
00:29:01,583 --> 00:29:04,042
Can't we just stay together like this?

278
00:29:04,346 --> 00:29:06,506
(TN: Everything he just said)
Please answer, Mr. Jang.

279
00:29:09,375 --> 00:29:10,875
You really were waiting for me here.

280
00:29:23,167 --> 00:29:24,958
Please answer me.

281
00:29:25,083 --> 00:29:26,417
Mr. Jang.

282
00:29:30,667 --> 00:29:32,250
(Continue Chatting)

283
00:29:32,375 --> 00:29:34,458
Was it all just in my head again?

284
00:30:08,125 --> 00:30:09,917
You win, Mr. Jang.

285
00:30:12,458 --> 00:30:13,875
I won't do this anymore.

286
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,625
I really won't.

287
00:30:20,708 --> 00:30:22,000
I was wrong.

288
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:53,167
Are you in so much pain because of me?

289
00:31:55,417 --> 00:31:58,500
"Boy, with Caution."

290
00:32:29,675 --> 00:32:30,758
Mr. Jang.

291
00:33:05,258 --> 00:33:08,633
If meeting me hadn't
brought you so much misery...

292
00:33:08,758 --> 00:33:10,092
Then...

293
00:33:18,758 --> 00:33:21,133
could we see each other again?
